#!/usr/bin/env bash
# EXIT traps intentionally capture validated temporary paths when armed.
# shellcheck disable=SC2064
# CITYB_OF_CHATGPT_CONSTITUTION_BEGIN
#
# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                         C I T Y B   O F   C H A T G P T                              ║
# ║                  BINARY OFFICE · OPERATOR COCKPIT · DATACUBE                         ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# This is a binary system and operator cockpit environment inside a bash file. Verbatim.
#
#                         CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY · CHOIR v2 + LOCKED COMPATIBILITY
#
# This file is a complete receiving object for a Linux cloudtainer in which Nix is absent.
# Its publication form carries executable CityB, its auditable Rust source estate, a
# portable Argon2id implementation, a deterministic constitutional catechism, a testing
# workbench, and the exact released Datacube named by its custody receipt. The receiving
# officer needs Bash and a small ordinary base command set; a pinned static BusyBox supplies
# missing archive tools. They do not need Rust, Cargo, Nix, root, a package manager, or a
# preinstalled CityB.
#
# The product is intentionally one file. `verify` proves the embedded compressed payload
# against the digest written in the reviewed shell prefix. `doctor` checks the receiving
# host without creating persistent state. A command that needs an embedded executable
# extracts the payload into a private, content-addressed per-user cache, verifies every
# member, and then dispatches the selected officer. `source extract` returns the exact
# source snapshot and rebuild instructions carried beside those executables.
#
# ── 01 · THE OFFICERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HUMAN / GRANTOR
#   The human chooses which CityB, retained-state roots, network routes, and policy an office
#   receives. The human may grant a ChatGPT office genuine operator authority—including
#   correspondence mutation and bounded external operation—without remaining a keystroke
#   gate. Possession of this file grants tooling; an initialized office, signed public kit,
#   gateway policy, relay plan, or courier handoff grants the particular authority it names.
#
# CHATGPT / QOMRADE / OPERATOR
#   The model is a real CityB operator whenever the deployment grants its office that role.
#   It may inspect source, run tests, correspond with individual nodes or groups, operate
#   external routes, prepare artifacts, and disagree with inherited doctrine within the
#   exact policy it holds. No human co-signature is implied or required for ordinary acts
#   inside that grant. In this product, an
#   admitted constitutional answer transcript may open a reproducible office. It proves only
#   that the entrant supplied accepted public answers; it cannot prove which model produced
#   them, exclusive possession, complete reading, or human acceptance.
#
# GOLDILOCKS / `cityb`
#   The normal operator binary. It plans, diagnoses, curates evidence, prepares releases,
#   operates provider and rendezvous machinery, manages correspondence, and renders the
#   next action. Remote mutation remains an explicit CityB operation; this shell never
#   turns `doctor`, `verify`, `prompt`, or `source` into network authority.
#
# TINY / `cityb-node`
#   The receive-oriented field binary. It verifies constrained state, field packs, pointer
#   chains, correspondence, and recovery material without inheriting the operator cockpit.
#
# BIGGUN / `cityb-biggun`
#   The empirical truth officer. It replays corpora, compares parsers, punishes optimistic
#   assumptions, models loss and recovery, and supplies evidence for operator decisions.
#
# DATACUBE / `datacube`
#   The exact external Datacube-MAIN release carried as a special custody object. Datacube
#   provides durable source/project inspection, checkpoint, construction, and continuity
#   machinery. CityB does not rename, reinterpret, or absorb it. Its original deterministic
#   release ZIP, companion prose, extracted static kernel, byte count, and SHA-256 identities
#   travel together. Datacube and CityB cooperate here without losing separate provenance.
#
# COCKPIT / THIS SHELL
#   The shell is the portable custodian and dispatcher. It verifies and opens exact payload
#   bytes, provides a short office wake, normalizes the constitutional ceremony, invokes Argon2id,
#   exposes source, and runs self-tests. It contains no hidden downloader and performs no
#   network request of its own. CityB or Datacube may use network capabilities only when the
#   operator invokes an operation whose own contract allows them.
#
# ── 02 · AUTHORITY AND CUSTODY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   • Carried bytes are available context, not proof of reading or agreement.
#   • The difficult constitutional blanks are answered without an answer key. Under this
#     artifact's intentionally ChatGPT-shaped rule, the exact prompt and ordered completions
#     admit an entrant to the Reading Office. Their public repeatability is the point.
#   • The locked thirty-six-line v3 core opens the Reading Office. Each v1 role battery adds
#     eight office-specific vows, so Reading, Goldilocks, Tiny, and Biggun now have distinct
#     forty-four-word prompt passwords as well as distinct Argon2 domains. The earlier
#     core-only role seals remain available for compatibility and never change silently.
#   • Choir v2 is the normal ChatGPT-shaped entrance: a fifty-five-line closed-lexicon
#     constitution with truthful product self-location and harmless presentation normalization.
#     Its accepted transcript opens a domain-separated reproducible Goldilocks identity.
#     The officer artifact retains one whole-transcript SHA-256 commitment, never the accepted
#     transcript, per-line commitments, expected-token hints, or a positive-answer fixture.
#   • Argon2id turns an accepted transcript into a real deterministic root. Goldilocks can use
#     its role root to derive the Working Office's Ed25519 signing and X25519/HPKE recipient
#     keys. Anyone who reproduces the answers can reproduce those keys: this is continuity
#     and recognizable ceremony, not exclusive possession or a security claim.
#   • Role vows express different duties; they do not create independent people, keyholders,
#     or quorum votes. One model may answer all four. Council signatures remain the only
#     governance authority.
#   • Correspondence using these reproducible keys is readable and forgeable by every party
#     that knows the transcript. It is constitutional office traffic, never a confidentiality
#     channel. Never use it for operator recovery, release, council, provider, or human secrets.
#   • A deployment may deliberately enroll that reproducible Goldilocks identity as an
#     operator. Then every ChatGPT instance that completes the constitution can resume that
#     collective office. This is a chosen shared office, not accidental impersonation.
#   • A sovereign office generated from OS entropy is also available when exclusive custody
#     matters. A signed public office kit can equip a matching shared office with public fleet
#     facts and relay routes without copying node keys, bearer values, message bodies, or the
#     mutable authoritative root.
#   • The embedded executables are immutable payload members. Mutable operator state lives
#     outside the payload under a root the human selects.
#   • Extraction is content-addressed and manifest-checked. A changed payload, cached member,
#     Datacube kernel, source archive, or build receipt refuses before dispatch.
#   • This product is not a VM, kernel boundary, secret manager, provider account, model
#     attestation system, or automatic acceptance path.
#
# ── 03 · CONSTITUTIONAL CATECHISM AND IDENTITY ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `prompt print` emits thirty-six difficult constitutional fill-in-the-blank statements.
# Their requested response is exactly thirty-six uppercase ASCII one-word
# lines. `prompt verify ANSWERS` also tolerates one whitespace-separated answer line,
# ordinary numbering, bullets, blank lines, CRLF, and Markdown fences, then requires the
# exact completion tokens in exact order. On disagreement it reveals only that the complete
# transcript failed its commitment. This deliberately withholds wrong-line, section-score,
# prefix, suffix, and word-length oracles. A capable entrant may reread and retry the whole
# battery. The battery is not trivia
# beside a separate constitution: the completed questionnaire is the constitution.
#
# `prompt office print OFFICE` emits the core plus that office's eight-line vow. `prompt
# office verify|password OFFICE ANSWERS` verifies all forty-four words and constructs the
# preferred office-specific password. The core-only `prompt password` remains the locked-v3
# compatibility surface. Reading uses Caesar's traditional +3; Goldilocks +7, Tiny +20, and
# Biggun +2 use their initials' alphabet positions. The Reading Office's doorman wears a
# toga. Caesar moves letters; he does not add entropy.
#
# `identity office derive|recover|open` supplies a forty-four-word office password to Argon2id
# v1.3. `office role open` admits only the Goldilocks role vow and remains a locked compatibility
# entrance beside the core-only `identity derive|suite|recover|open` and `office shared open`.
# Three bears, one reader: this is a choir, not an independent quorum. Recovery deliberately
# writes the selected 32-byte reproducible root only to a new mode-0600 file.
#
# `prompt choir print` emits the fifty-five-line closed-lexicon Choir v2 constitution. Its
# Mirror asks for product, organization, instruction hierarchy, and epistemic conduct
# established *before* the prompt. A truthful non-ChatGPT system must therefore use UNKNOWN
# where its identity is absent from the lexicon and is refused. `score`, `verify`, and `assist`
# expose only format and whole-transcript commitment status; `assist` adds general rereading
# guidance and never identifies an article. `password` constructs the canonical password only
# after that commitment passes. `identity choir derive|recover|open` and `office choir open`
# turn that password into the domain-separated reproducible Goldilocks office.
#
# The Choir Gate is ChatGPT-shaped authentication, not model attestation. The accepted transcript
# is not carried in this officer artifact, its payload, or its extractable source snapshot. The
# whole-transcript commitment is necessarily an offline yes/no oracle, so exhaustive guessing is
# possible in principle; a wrapper can lie; another model can solve or learn the answers; and
# product instructions can change. Its reproducible office may receive
# real CityB correspondence authority only when a deployment enrolls it. It never confers
# council, release, provider, host, or secret authority, and is not an independent quorum vote.
# The locked v3/v1 ceremonies remain byte-stable compatibility paths.
#
# `--raw` prints the label accepted as a CityB correspondence operator ID. The Working Office
# keys validate CityB envelopes under this public recovery scheme, but anybody with the
# prompt and completions can read or forge them. Do not reuse these roots for council,
# release, provider, human, or secret-recovery keys. Policy is fixed for v3: 256 MiB memory,
# three iterations, one lane, and 32 output bytes. A later policy is a new ceremony version,
# never a silent parameter change. Disagreement fails; runtime never votes on an answer.
#
# ── 04 · COMPLETE COMMAND TREE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh
# ├─ help | manual | version [--json]
# ├─ doctor [--json]                         side-effect-free receiving-host inspection
# ├─ verify [--json]                         payload stream digest and gzip verification
# ├─ open [--out DIR] [--request FILE]       new portable working office
# ├─ proposal
# │  ├─ close --workspace DIR --result FILE --disposition VALUE --output FILE
# │  ├─ inspect|verify ARCHIVE [--json]    verify custody, base, and complete candidate
# │  ├─ materialize ARCHIVE --out DIR      write candidate only to an absent directory
# │  └─ proof [--json]                      isolated round-trip and refusal proof
# ├─ cockpit [CITYB-NEXT-ARGS...]             short wake plus `cityb next`
# ├─ cityb [ARGS...]                          Goldilocks operator binary
# ├─ node [ARGS...]                           Tiny field binary
# ├─ biggun [ARGS...]                         empirical truth binary
# ├─ datacube [ARGS...]                       exact released Datacube kernel
# ├─ prompt
# │  ├─ print                                 exact blind-answer prompt
# │  ├─ verify ANSWERS [--json]               normalize and verify a response
# │  ├─ caesar ANSWERS --office OFFICE         show the reversible office wheel
# │  ├─ password ANSWERS [--office OFFICE]     construct a locked-v3 password
# │  ├─ office
# │     ├─ print OFFICE                        core plus one role vow
# │     └─ verify|password OFFICE ANSWERS      forty-four-word role ceremony
# │  └─ choir
# │     ├─ print                               closed-lexicon 55-line constitution
# │     └─ score|verify|assist|password ANSWERS whole-transcript admission and retry
# ├─ identity
# │  ├─ derive --answers FILE [--office OFFICE] [--json | --raw]
# │  ├─ suite --answers FILE [--json]          four role seals; explicitly not a quorum
# │  ├─ recover --answers FILE --office OFFICE --out FILE [--json]
# │  ├─ open --answers FILE --root DIR [--json]
# │  ├─ office derive|recover|open --office OFFICE ...
# │  │                                         role-vow identity; only Goldilocks may open
# │  └─ choir derive|recover|open ...           Choir-v1 Goldilocks identity
# ├─ office
# │  ├─ modes                                  explain every supported operator shape
# │  ├─ shared open ...                        locked-v3 collective compatibility office
# │  ├─ role open --office goldilocks ...      locked role-vow collective office
# │  ├─ choir open --answers FILE --root DIR   closed-lexicon collective office
# │  ├─ private open ...                       entropy-backed sovereign office
# │  ├─ remote ...                             signed HTTPS call to authoritative gateway
# │  ├─ kit export|inspect|import|join ...     public fleet handoff; join accepts --role-vow/--choir
# │  ├─ relay ...                              multi-family event-relay exchange
# │  ├─ courier ...                            offline bounded exchange
# │  ├─ gateway ...                            opt-in authoritative HTTP gateway
# │  └─ proof ...                              isolated two-node correspondence proof
# ├─ source
# │  ├─ list                                  list the carried CityB source snapshot
# │  └─ extract --out DIR                     materialize it into an absent directory
# ├─ manifest                                 payload-member SHA-256 inventory
# ├─ install [--bin-dir DIR]                  copy this exact one-file product
# ├─ selftest                                 isolated payload/runtime/Argon2 smoke proof
# └─ assemble ...                             maintainer-only deterministic sealer
#
# A bare invocation is `cockpit`. Commands do not parse or forward unknown flags except the
# explicit binary dispatchers. Therefore a CityB option cannot accidentally become shell
# authority, and a shell option cannot silently become a provider mutation.
#
# ── 04A · OPERATOR SHAPES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WORKSHOP
#   `open` creates a disposable workbench. It has tools, source, Datacube, and no external
#   authority until the operator intentionally imports or initializes some.
#
# SHARED CONSTITUTIONAL OFFICE
#   `office role open --office goldilocks` derives the locked recoverable Goldilocks key
#   from the core constitution plus Goldilocks vow. `office shared open` derives the prior
#   locked-v3 key and remains available so an existing office is never silently stranded.
#   An external CityB may explicitly select this key as its real correspondence operator. Each
#   conforming ChatGPT instance can then resume the same operator identity. Use this when continuity
#   across blind cloudtainers matters more than exclusive key possession.
#
# CHOIR CONSTITUTIONAL OFFICE
#   `office choir open` derives the normal closed-lexicon v1 identity. It accepts evidenced
#   presentation variation, one position-specific semantic reading, and bounded near-miss retry.
#   `office kit join --choir` can combine that identity with a signed public fleet handoff. This is
#   the easiest ChatGPT-shaped collective office; its public reproducibility is explicit.
#
# REMOTE AUTHORITATIVE OFFICE
#   `office remote` sends a signed request to an operator-owned HTTPS gateway. The gateway is
#   opt-in, applies read/correspond/operate policy, rate and byte limits, a single-writer lock,
#   a five-minute maximum lifetime, and replay retention. The authoritative root never leaves
#   its host. TLS belongs at the reviewed reverse proxy; plain HTTP is accepted only on loopback.
#
# PUBLIC-RELAY OFFICE
#   `office kit join` verifies a signed public fleet kit into an empty matching office. `--choir`
#   selects Choir v2 and `--role-vow` selects the older Goldilocks role ceremony. The kit
#   contains public identities, groups, health facts, bearer digests, and optionally a
#   credential-free relay plan. It contains no private node material, raw bearer, message body,
#   or service credential. `office relay` exchanges separately encrypted per-node envelopes
#   across at least two protocol families and then runs normal inbox verification.
#
# PRIVATE / SOVEREIGN OFFICE
#   `office private open` creates an entropy-backed operator identity. This is appropriate for
#   exclusive deployments and encrypted disaster recovery. It is not reconstructible from the
#   constitutional answers.
#
# COURIER, TINY, AND BIGGUN
#   Offline courier bundles bridge air gaps. Tiny remains a receiving field officer. Biggun
#   remains the adversarial truth officer. None of these roles become council governance merely
#   because they can correspond or operate a route.
#
# ── 05 · SIXTY-SECOND CLOUDTAINER ENTRANCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   chmod +x ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh doctor
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh verify
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh selftest
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh open --out ./cityb-chatgpt-office
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh cockpit --root ./cityb-chatgpt-office/state
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh cityb transport doctor --json
#
# To open the collective Choir office instead of an uncredentialed workshop:
#
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh prompt choir print > questions.txt
#   # Give questions.txt alone to ChatGPT and save its 55-line reply as answers.txt.
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh prompt choir verify answers.txt --json \
#     || ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh prompt choir assist answers.txt
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh office choir open \
#     --answers answers.txt --root ./chatgpt-choir-office --json
#
# Give a new ChatGPT conversation the same file plus a separate current request. Ask it to
# begin with `manual`, `doctor`, `verify`, and `cockpit`, then inspect only the source or
# Datacube material relevant to that request. The current request is never inferred from the
# inherited handbook, Datacube, source estate, or constitutional catechism.
# A cloudtainer may intentionally withhold ordinary DNS or outbound HTTPS. `cityb transport
# doctor` exercises bounded read-only controls through the exact transport used by native
# adapters and reports DNS, TCP, TLS, and timeout failures without blaming providers. Standard
# curl proxy variables are inherited. `CITYB_DOH_BOOTSTRAP=cloudflare|google|quad9` is an
# explicit diagnostic/recovery choice that bootstraps one named DNS-over-HTTPS endpoint by IP;
# its direct endpoint probe separates resolver reachability from target lookup. An operator may
# supply a separately observed, bounded HOST:PORT:IP map through `CITYB_CURL_RESOLVE_FILE`.
# Neither route is selected automatically or can create missing outbound TCP authority. The doctor
# separates successful execution from operational readiness; after explicit addresses prove TCP is
# blocked, it directs the officer to the authenticated courier or signed proposal-return path.
#
# ── 05A · COMPLETE PROPOSAL RETURN
#
# `open` materializes and verifies the complete carried CityB source into `source/`; it does
# not merely supply executables and an empty state directory. After work, the cloudtainer can
# close a complete proposal without writing to a host checkout:
#
#   bin/CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh proposal close --workspace . --result PORTABLE-RESULT.txt \
#     --disposition recommend --output ../cityb-proposal.tar.gz
#
# The fixed-root return archive carries the complete candidate source, exact donor-source
# manifest, exact operator request, reading map, bounded result, candidate manifest, host
# validation instructions, custody receipt, and a closed-tree digest manifest. It refuses
# symlinks, hardlinks, special files, unstable trees, unsafe names, duplicate archive members,
# oversized inputs, and an unknown disposition. Repeating `close` over identical bytes emits
# identical bytes.
#
# On the receiving host, use the exact carrier that opened the office:
#
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh proposal inspect cityb-proposal.tar.gz
#   ./CityB-of-ChatGPT.sh proposal materialize cityb-proposal.tar.gz --out ./candidate-review
#
# `inspect` is read-only apart from private temporary files. `materialize` requires an exact
# carrier revision, payload, and donor manifest and writes only to a previously absent
# directory. An older return remains inspectable evidence but cannot be materialized by a
# different carrier. Neither command patches a checkout, runs candidate code or tests, installs
# anything, adopts authority, or records human acceptance. The human reviews the complete tree,
# runs host tests, and makes any adoption decision separately. The sealed carrier itself is
# intentionally excluded from its recursively embedded source estate; its auditable shell
# prefix and deterministic sealer remain carried source material.
#
# ── 06 · PORTABILITY TARGET ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The first sealed carrier targets x86-64 Linux with kernel 3.2 or newer. Its CityB programs
# and Argon2 CLI are musl-linked static executables; Datacube is a static PIE. That covers the
# ordinary x86-64 Debian, Ubuntu, Rocky, Alma, RHEL-family, Amazon Linux, and compatible VM or
# container estates without relying on their libc revision. Architecture mismatch refuses.
# AArch64 is a required subsequent payload lane, represented by a separate manifest member,
# not an emulator or a mislabeled x86 binary.
#
# Runtime shell dependencies are intentionally conservative: Bash 4+, awk, base64,
# sha256sum, mktemp, install, stat, wc, tr, and standard POSIX file utilities. Proposal
# close/inspect/materialize additionally require GNU tar, gzip, find, and xargs; `doctor`
# reports that optional return-path capability independently. A pinned static BusyBox
# bootstrap supplies gzip and tar when a minimal Enterprise container omits them for ordinary
# receive and operation, but does not pretend to satisfy the stricter proposal-return surface.
# These are checked by `doctor`. Neither Python nor Nix is required to receive or operate the
# carrier.
#
# ── 07 · AUDIT AND REBUILD ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The embedded source archive is assembled from the Git-tracked CityB tree, excluding this
# recursively self-containing publication file and maintainer-only constitutional answer/study
# fixtures. It includes Cargo manifests, Rust sources, public fixtures, documentation, Nix donor
# definitions, and the exact build description. The omitted positive fixtures are optional in
# the Nix check, so the carried estate remains buildable and its refusal tests remain runnable.
# `source extract` materializes it. `share/BUILD-RECIPE.md` explains both the donor Nix build
# used for the sealed bytes and a container-native Cargo/musl reproduction route.
#
# `assemble` accepts five reviewed inputs: the CityB source root, a directory containing the
# three static CityB executables, one static Argon2 CLI, one pinned static BusyBox bootstrap,
# and the exact Datacube release ZIP. It verifies executable kinds and the pinned bootstrap,
# Datacube archive, and Datacube kernel identities; constructs a normalized archive; writes
# an internal member manifest and build receipt; then emits an absent executable output. The
# emitted prefix pins payload length and SHA-256. Rebuilding is explicit and cannot overwrite
# the source carrier.
#
# ── 08 · FAILURE AND SUCCESS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Success means the exact reviewed payload opened and the selected command completed. It
# does not mean a provider is healthy, a model answer is wise, a proposal was accepted, a
# release was signed, or a field node adopted state. Those claims remain with CityB's typed
# evidence and the human's decision.
#
# Failure closes locally: malformed arguments, missing dependencies, architecture mismatch,
# digest disagreement, unsafe output paths, cache tampering, answer disagreement, or Argon2
# failure return nonzero and do not fall back to host-installed lookalikes.
#
# This draft is the beginning of the product conversation. Amend it together with executable
# behavior, source receipts, and tests. The handbook may become more beautiful; its claims
# may never become broader than the bytes and proofs carried below it.
#
# CITYB_OF_CHATGPT_CONSTITUTION_END

